                  <line x1="16" y1="2" x2="16" y2="6"></line>
                  <line x1="8" y1="2" x2="8" y2="6"></line>
                  <line x1="3" y1="10" x2="21" y2="10"></line>
                </svg>
                {new Date(article.date).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })}
              </span>
              <span class="stat-item">
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
                  <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
                  <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"></polyline>
                </svg>
                {article.readingTime}
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Article Cover -->
      <div class="article-cover">
        <img 
          src={article.cover} 
          alt={article.title}
          class="article-cover-image"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
      
      <!-- Article Content -->
      <div class="article-body">
        <div class="container-narrow">
          <div class="article-content">
            <h2>Understanding Your Skin</h2>
            <p>Building an effective skincare routine starts with understanding your unique skin type and its specific needs. Whether you have dry, oily, combination, or sensitive skin, the right approach can make all the difference in achieving that healthy, radiant glow.</p>
            
            <p>In this comprehensive guide, we'll walk you through the essential steps of creating a personalized skincare routine that works for you. From cleansing to moisturizing, each step plays a crucial role in maintaining skin health and addressing specific concerns.</p>
            
            <h3>The Essential Steps</h3>
            <p>A basic skincare routine consists of three fundamental steps that should be performed twice daily - morning and evening:</p>
            
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Cleansing:</strong> Remove dirt, oil, and impurities that accumulate on your skin throughout the day.</li>
              <li><strong>Toning:</strong> Balance your skin's pH levels and prepare it for better absorption of subsequent products.</li>
              <li><strong>Moisturizing:</strong> Hydrate and protect your skin barrier to maintain optimal skin health.</li>
            </ol>
            
            <h3>Morning vs. Evening Routine</h3>
            <p>Your morning routine should focus on protection, while your evening routine emphasizes repair and renewal. In the morning, always finish with sunscreen (SPF 30 or higher) to protect against UV damage. At night, consider incorporating treatment products like serums or retinol to address specific skin concerns.</p>
            
            <blockquote>
              <p>"Consistency is key in skincare. Results don't happen overnight, but with patience and the right routine, you'll see significant improvements in your skin's health and appearance."</p>
              <cite>— Dr. Sarah Mitchell, Medical Director</cite>
            </blockquote>
            
            <h3>Choosing the Right Products</h3>
            <p>When selecting skincare products, look for ingredients that address your specific concerns. For anti-aging, consider products with retinol, vitamin C, or peptides. For acne-prone skin, salicylic acid and niacinamide can be beneficial. Always patch test new products and introduce them gradually into your routine.</p>
            
            <p>Remember, expensive doesn't always mean better. Focus on products with proven ingredients and formulations that work for your skin type. Consult with a dermatologist or skincare professional if you're unsure about what's right for you.</p>
            
            <h3>Common Mistakes to Avoid</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Over-exfoliating or using too many active ingredients at once</li>
              <li>Skipping sunscreen, even on cloudy days</li>
              <li>Not removing makeup before bed</li>
              <li>Using products that are too harsh for your skin type</li>
              <li>Expecting immediate results and switching products too quickly</li>
            </ul>
            
            <p>Building a skincare routine is a journey, not a destination. Be patient with your skin, listen to its needs, and adjust your routine as necessary. With consistent care and the right products, you'll be well on your way to achieving the healthy, glowing skin you deserve.</p>
          </div>
          
